# {{agent_name}}

{{agent_description}}

A **Buzz agent**: an ACP-speaking agent with a Nostr identity that can join a
Buzz relay. No web framework, no framework SDK — configuration is read from
the environment and the model loop is plain HTTP against an OpenAI-compatible
endpoint.

## Quickstart

```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env        # then fill in OPENROUTER_API_KEY
export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)

python -m {{agent_package}}.cli "hello"
```

## Entrypoints

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `python -m {{agent_package}}.cli "…"` | one-shot prompt from the terminal |
| `python -m {{agent_package}}.cli` | interactive REPL |
| `python -m {{agent_package}}.acp` | ACP subprocess (stdio JSON-RPC) for editors |
| `python -m {{agent_package}}.buzz_relay` | join a Buzz relay group and reply in chat |

All four drive the same `AgentRuntime`, so tools, skills, and model config
behave identically whichever way a turn arrives.

## Configuration

Every knob is an environment variable; see [.env.example](.env.example) for the
annotated list. The ones you can't skip:

| Env | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `BUZZ_AGENT_PROVIDER` | `openrouter` (default), `openai`, `anthropic`, `groq`, `together`, `ollama` |
| `BUZZ_AGENT_MODEL` | model id (provider prefix optional) |
| `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` | provider key — or the key env matching your provider |
| `BUZZ_RELAY_URL` | relay WebSocket URL (relay worker only) |
| `BUZZ_GROUP_ID` | NIP-29 group id to join (relay worker only) |

## Editor integration (ACP)

[ACP](https://agentclientprotocol.com) is the JSON-RPC-over-stdio protocol
editors like Zed use to talk to agents. The adapter handles `initialize` →
`session/new` → `session/prompt`, streams `session/update` notifications
(`agent_message_chunk`, `agent_thought_chunk`, `tool_call`,
`tool_call_update`), and honors `session/cancel` mid-turn. stdout carries
protocol traffic only — all logging goes to stderr.

To register it in Zed, add an entry under `agent_servers` pointing `command`
at `python` and `args` at `["-m", "{{agent_package}}.acp"]`, with `cwd` set to
this project. Run `nuvel doctor` from this directory to smoke-test the stdio
handshake and print a ready-to-paste snippet.

## Nostr identity

The agent signs everything it publishes with a Nostr key (BIP-340 Schnorr over
secp256k1, implemented in `{{agent_package}}/nostr_identity.py` — no crypto
dependency).

- Set `NOSTR_PRIVATE_KEY` (hex or `nsec1…`) to pin an identity, **or**
- leave it unset: a key is generated on first run and persisted to
  `NOSTR_KEY_FILE` (default `.nostr/identity.json`, mode `0600`, gitignored).

Print the public identity at any time:

```bash
python -m {{agent_package}}.nostr_identity
```

## Skills

Skills live in `{{agent_package}}/skills/<slug>/SKILL.md` (Anthropic skills
format: YAML frontmatter with `name` + `description`, then the body). The agent
sees every skill's description up front and reads a body on demand via the
`read_skill` tool — drop a directory in and it's live on the next run.

`buzz_persona.py` renders those same skills into the Buzz persona/profile
(Nostr kind-0 metadata) the relay publishes, so what the agent advertises in
chat stays in sync with what it can actually do.

## Tools

Add a tool by returning a `Tool` from your own module and passing it to
`build_agent(extra_tools=[...])`, or extend `skill_tools()` in
`{{agent_package}}/skills/__init__.py`:

```python
from {{agent_package}}.agent import Tool

Tool(
    name="get_status",
    description="Look up the current status of a job.",
    parameters={
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {"job_id": {"type": "string"}},
        "required": ["job_id"],
    },
    handler=get_status,          # sync or async
)
```

Handlers may be sync or async and receive decoded arguments as keyword
arguments; whatever they return is JSON-encoded back to the model.
